WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:04.191
Imagine a user clicks submit twice or a response is lost

00:00:04.249 --> 00:00:05.689
after the server saves the record.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.626
The client may not know whether a retry will create a

00:00:08.673 --> 00:00:09.230
duplicate.

00:00:09.671 --> 00:00:13.375
The design can use an operation identifier, a uniqueness

00:00:13.444 --> 00:00:16.869
rule, or another suitable method; the correct choice

00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:18.692
depends on the existing system.

00:00:19.203 --> 00:00:22.546
Document the intended effect and how an uncertain outcome

00:00:22.569 --> 00:00:23.556
will be reconciled.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:27.736
"Just retry" is not enough when an operation can send a

00:00:27.806 --> 00:00:31.219
message, charge money, or create a duplicate record.
